message.content:
Now I see the key issue. In the "Build the isolate_level connections" section:

```c
prev_isolate_level = 0;
for_run_list (pp, main_run_list)
{
  int isolate_level = RL_ISOLATE_LEVEL (pp);
  int i;

  if (isolate_level<prev_isolate_level)
    for (i=isolate_level+1; i<=prev_isolate_level; i++)
      run_per_isolate_level[i]=0;
  prev_isolate_level = isolate_level;

  if (run_per_isolate_level[isolate_level])
    {
      run_per_isolate_level[isolate_level]->next_isolate = pp;
      pp->prev_isolate = run_per_isolate_level[isolate_level];
    }
  run_per_isolate_level[isolate_level] = pp;
}
```

If `isolate_level` becomes negative (e.g., -1), then `run_per_isolate_level[-1]` is an out-of-bounds access (before the array). This is the memory-safety bug.

Also `last_strong_stack[iso_level]` in the weak types section would be an OOB access if iso_level is negative.

So the vulnerability: `isolate_level` can be decreased below zero. Let me confirm the mechanism.

The `isolate_level` is incremented only when `< FRIBIDI_BIDI_MAX_EXPLICIT_LEVEL-1`. Let me check the value of `FRIBIDI_BIDI_MAX_EXPLICIT_LEVEL`.

